# Versioning

App version lives in `pubspec.yaml` as `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH+BUILD`.

The `+BUILD` number is the Android `versionCode` when `force-version-code-ignoring-abi` is enabled (arm64 sideload builds).

## When to bump what

| Change | Bump | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| **New feature** (including small ones) | **minor** — reset patch to 0 | 1.2.0 → **1.3.0** |
| **Bug fix** | **patch** | 1.3.0 → **1.3.1** |
| Typos, chores, copy tweaks, refactors with no behavior change | **build** only | 1.3.1+10 → 1.3.1+**11** |
| Breaking / major rewrite | **major** | 1.3.1 → **2.0.0** |

Command: `dart run scripts/bump_version.dart [major|minor|patch|build]` (use `scripts/flutter.bat` on Windows).

## Cursor agent sessions

Before finishing, write the bump type so the **stop** hook can apply it when `lib/` was edited:

- `echo minor > .cursor/.bump-type` — features
- `echo patch > .cursor/.bump-type` — fixes
- `echo build > .cursor/.bump-type` — chores (default if omitted)

The stop hook runs `scripts/hooks/bump_on_stop.dart` only when `.cursor/.bump-pending` exists (set by the afterFileEdit hook on `lib/**/*.dart` edits).

## Git commits

With hooks installed (`scripts/install_git_hooks.sh`), `.githooks/commit-msg` bumps from the message prefix when `lib/` or `test/` changed:

- `feat:` → minor
- `fix:` → patch
- anything else → build only

Skips bump if `pubspec.yaml` is already staged.
